{"files":[{"content":"#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n#include <string.h>\n#include <stddef.h>\n#include <stdint.h>\n\n/* Maximum size (in char) for neighbors and compute lists */\n#define MAX 100\n\ntypedef struct {\n  int id;\n  float value;\n} Node;\n\ntypedef struct {\n  int *keys;\n  int *indices;\n  size_t capacity;\n} IdIndex;\n\ntypedef struct {\n  float value;\n  unsigned char ready;\n} CostEntry;\n\ntypedef struct {\n  int node;\n  int successor;\n} PathEntry;\n\n/* Reads input, allocates compact node records and separate neighbor text. */\nNode* read_input(char* fname, int *n, char* list, char **neighbor_data) {\n  Node* data = NULL;\n  FILE *fl = NULL;\n\n  *neighbor_data = NULL;\n  if (fname == NULL)\n    fl = stdin;\n  else\n    fl = fopen(fname, \"r\");\n\n  if (fl == NULL) {\n    fprintf(stderr, \"Error!\\n\");\n    exit(1);\n  }\n\n  list[0] = '\\0';\n  fscanf(fl, \"%d%99[^\\n]\", n, list);\n\n  if (*n > 0) {\n    size_t count = (size_t)*n;\n    size_t max_size = (size_t)-1;\n    if (count > max_size / sizeof(*data) || count > max_size / MAX) {\n      fprintf(stderr, \"Error!\\n\");\n      fclose(fl);\n      exit(1);\n    }\n    data = (Node*)malloc(count * sizeof(*data));\n    *neighbor_data = (char*)malloc(count * MAX);\n    if (data == NULL || *neighbor_data == NULL) {\n      fprintf(stderr, \"Error!\\n\");\n      free(data);\n      free(*neighbor_data);\n      fclose(fl);\n      exit(1);\n    }\n  }\n\n  for (int i = 0; i < *n; i++) {\n    char *neighbors = *neighbor_data + (size_t)i * MAX;\n    neighbors[0] = '\\0';\n    fscanf(fl, \"%d %f%99[^\\n]\", &data[i].id, &data[i].value, neighbors);\n  }\n\n  fclose(fl);\n  return data;\n}\n\n/* Mix an integer ID before masking it into the power-of-two table. */\nstatic size_t hash_id(int id) {\n  uint32_t x = (uint32_t)id;\n  x ^= x >> 16;\n  x *= UINT32_C(0x7feb352d);\n  x ^= x >> 15;\n  x *= UINT32_C(0x846ca68b);\n  x ^= x >> 16;\n  return (size_t)x;\n}\n\n/* Build an open-addressed index, retaining the first occurrence of each ID. */\nstatic void build_id_index(IdIndex *index, const Node *g, int size) {\n  index->keys = NULL;\n  index->indices = NULL;\n  index->capacity = 0;\n\n  if (size <= 0)\n    return;\n\n  size_t max_size = (size_t)-1;\n  size_t count = (size_t)size;\n  if (count > max_size / 2) {\n    fprintf(stderr, \"Error!\\n\");\n    exit(1);\n  }\n\n  size_t needed = count * 2;\n  size_t capacity = 1;\n  while (capacity < needed) {\n    if (capacity > max_size / 2) {\n      fprintf(stderr, \"Error!\\n\");\n      exit(1);\n    }\n    capacity *= 2;\n  }\n  if (capacity > max_size / sizeof(int)) {\n    fprintf(stderr, \"Error!\\n\");\n    exit(1);\n  }\n\n  index->keys = (int*)malloc(capacity * sizeof(*index->keys));\n  index->indices = (int*)malloc(capacity * sizeof(*index->indices));\n  if (index->keys == NULL || index->indices == NULL) {\n    fprintf(stderr, \"Error!\\n\");\n    free(index->keys);\n    free(index->indices);\n    exit(1);\n  }\n  index->capacity = capacity;\n\n  for (size_t i = 0; i < capacity; i++)\n    index->indices[i] = -1;\n\n  size_t mask = capacity - 1;\n  for (int i = 0; i < size; i++) {\n    size_t slot = hash_id(g[i].id) & mask;\n    while (index->indices[slot] != -1 && index->keys[slot] != g[i].id)\n      slot = (slot + 1) & mask;\n    if (index->indices[slot] == -1) {\n      index->keys[slot] = g[i].id;\n      index->indices[slot] = i;\n    }\n  }\n}\n\n/* Returns the first index of the node with the given ID, or -1 if absent. */\nstatic int find_by_id(const IdIndex *index, int id) {\n  if (index->capacity == 0)\n    return -1;\n\n  size_t mask = index->capacity - 1;\n  size_t slot = hash_id(id) & mask;\n  int found = index->indices[slot];\n  if (found == -1)\n    return -1;\n  if (index->keys[slot] == id)\n    return found;\n\n  slot = (slot + 1) & mask;\n  for (;;) {\n    int first_event = 4;\n#ifdef _OPENMP\n#pragma omp simd reduction(min:first_event)\n#endif\n    for (int lane = 0; lane < 4; lane++) {\n      size_t candidate = (slot + (size_t)lane) & mask;\n      int candidate_index = index->indices[candidate];\n      int event = (candidate_index == -1 || index->keys[candidate] == id) ? lane : 4;\n      first_event = event < first_event ? event : first_event;\n    }\n\n    if (first_event < 4) {\n      size_t candidate = (slot + (size_t)first_event) & mask;\n      int candidate_index = index->indices[candidate];\n      return candidate_index == -1 ? -1 : candidate_index;\n    }\n    slot = (slot + 4) & mask;\n  }\n}\n\n/* Select the same highest-valued neighbor as the recursive reference routine. */\nstatic int selected_successor(const Node *g, const char *neighbor_data,\n                              int node, const IdIndex *index) {\n  char aux[MAX];\n  char *saveptr = NULL;\n  int idmax = -1;\n  int successor = -1;\n  float max = 0.0f;\n\n  strcpy(aux, neighbor_data + (size_t)node * MAX);\n  char *token = strtok_r(aux, \" \", &saveptr);\n  while (token != NULL) {\n    int neighbor_id = atoi(token);\n    int d = find_by_id(index, neighbor_id);\n    if (d >= 0 && max < g[d].value) {\n      max = g[d].value;\n      idmax = neighbor_id;\n      successor = neighbor_id != -1 ? d : -1;\n    }\n    token = strtok_r(NULL, \" \", &saveptr);\n  }\n\n  /* The original routine uses -1 as its no-successor sentinel. */\n  return idmax == -1 ? -1 : successor;\n}\n\n/* Evaluate an unresolved selected-successor path tail-first and memoize it. */\nstatic float get_costly(Node *g, const char *neighbor_data, int id,\n                        const IdIndex *index, CostEntry *cache,\n                        PathEntry *path) {\n  int root = find_by_id(index, id);\n  if (root < 0)\n    return 0.0f;\n  if (cache[root].ready)\n    return cache[root].value;\n\n  int path_length = 0;\n  int current = root;\n  while (current >= 0 && !cache[current].ready) {\n    int successor = selected_successor(g, neighbor_data, current, index);\n    path[path_length].node = current;\n    path[path_length].successor = successor;\n    path_length++;\n    current = successor;\n  }\n\n  while (path_length > 0) {\n    PathEntry entry = path[--path_length];\n    float value = g[entry.node].value;\n    if (entry.successor >= 0)\n      value += cache[entry.successor].value;\n    cache[entry.node].value = value;\n    cache[entry.node].ready = 1;\n  }\n\n  return cache[root].value;\n}\n\n/* Main program - reads input, computes sums, and prints output. */\nint main(void) {\n  char *fileN = NULL;\n  char computelist[MAX];\n  char *neighbor_data = NULL;\n  int n = -1;\n\n  Node *input = read_input(fileN, &n, computelist, &neighbor_data);\n  IdIndex index;\n  build_id_index(&index, input, n);\n\n  size_t allocation_count = n > 0 ? (size_t)n : 1;\n  CostEntry *cache = (CostEntry*)calloc(allocation_count, sizeof(*cache));\n  PathEntry *path = (PathEntry*)malloc(allocation_count * sizeof(*path));\n  if (cache == NULL || path == NULL) {\n    fprintf(stderr, \"Error!\\n\");\n    free(cache);\n    free(path);\n    free(index.keys);\n    free(index.indices);\n    free(neighbor_data);\n    free(input);\n    return 1;\n  }\n\n  for (char *c = strtok(computelist, \" \"); c != NULL; c = strtok(NULL, \" \"))\n    printf(\"%s: %f\\n\", c,\n           get_costly(input, neighbor_data, atoi(c), &index, cache, path));\n\n  free(path);\n  free(cache);\n  free(index.keys);\n  free(index.indices);\n  free(neighbor_data);\n  free(input);\n  return 0;\n}\n","path":"src/graph.c"}],"hypothesis":"Combining open-addressed ID lookup and tail-first per-node cost memoization should reduce repeated scans while preserving first-match lookup and float addition order. Compacting node records and separating neighbor text may also improve locality during sparse value lookups.","notes":"No commands were run. The candidate uses only the archived hash/memoization and compact-node/neighbor-buffer ideas; correctness and performance remain for the controller to evaluate.","research":{"queries":[],"urls":[]},"sources_kept":["96528732a76e42fd","0cfc47332129405f"],"transformations":["Use split key and node-index arrays in an open-addressed ID table, checking the home bucket first and probing collision candidates in groups of four for the earliest match or empty slot; preserve first-occurrence behavior for duplicate IDs.","Memoize per-node costs and evaluate unresolved selected-successor paths tail-first so float accumulation order matches recursive evaluation.","Keep compact ID/value node records and store fixed-size neighbor text in a separate contiguous buffer; allocate records for every positive node count."]}